-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §44: the conversion formula — X, the salary
-- to convert (a 100% position's pay in the components listed, in March of
-- the year before the move); Y, the conversion coefficient by status and
-- the school the teacher will work in, weighted where he worked on two
-- position bases; and A = X × (100 + Y)%.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `44`

§§ `44(א) X, the salary to convert`

DECLARE `the teacher's state in the determining month` IS ONE OF
    `at work`
    `on unpaid leave, a sabbatical or another unpaid permitted absence`
    `on reserve duty or maternity leave`

DECLARE `month of the salary to convert` IS ONE OF
    `March of the school year before the move`
    `September of the year of the move, as if off the reform`

-- (א)(1): the pay of a 100% position by the teacher's roles, in the March
-- salary of the year before the move ("החודש הקובע"), in the components of
-- (ב) only; (2): one on unpaid leave or a sabbatical on the eve of the move
-- by the September of the year of the move, as if off the reform; (3): one
-- on reserve duty or maternity leave in March by the pay he would have had.
@ref akn:art_44__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_44__para_a__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_44__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_44__para_a__subpara_3
GIVEN s IS A `the teacher's state in the determining month`
GIVETH A `month of the salary to convert`
DECIDE `the month X is taken from` s IS
    IF s EQUALS `on unpaid leave, a sabbatical or another unpaid permitted absence`
    THEN `September of the year of the move, as if off the reform`
    ELSE `March of the school year before the move`

§§ `44(ב) The components of X`

DECLARE `pay component` IS ONE OF
    `the combined salary`
    `the 1987 supplement`
    `the 1994 supplement`
    `the 2001 supplement`
    `the 2008 supplement (agreement of 22.1.08)`
    `a role allowance that does not go on under this agreement`
    `the training allowance`
    `the double-degree allowance`
    `the minimum-wage supplement`
    `the cost-of-living supplement, where not in other components, as agreed`
    `a component agreed later to be in X`
    `a trailing management or counselling allowance`
    `the management allowance of a former principal not entitled to trail it`
    `a role allowance §39 keeps`
    `the counselling allowance`
    `another component`

-- (ב)(1): the list; ¶13: for the teachers of §10(א)–(ב), §10(ג) applies.
-- (2): a trailing management or counselling allowance is in X; (3): a
-- former principal's management allowance he is not entitled to trail is
-- not.
@ref akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p4 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p5 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p6 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p7 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p8 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p9 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p10 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p11 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p12 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_1/p13 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_3
GIVEN c IS A `pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the salary to convert` c IF
    NOT (   c EQUALS `the management allowance of a former principal not entitled to trail it`
         OR c EQUALS `a role allowance §39 keeps`
         OR c EQUALS `the counselling allowance`
         OR c EQUALS `another component`)

DECLARE `when the entitlement was completed` IS ONE OF
    `by March of the year before the move`
    `between March and 1 September of the year of the move`
    `between 1 September and 31 December of the year of the move`
    `between 1.1.08 and 31.8.08, the teacher having moved in 5768`
    `later`

DECLARE `how a new degree or training allowance counts` IS ONE OF
    `in X from the start`
    `in X by a second conversion, from the date of the entitlement`
    `not in X`

-- (ב)(4)–(6): a degree or training allowance completed after March and
-- before 1 September is in X; one completed by 31 December of the year of
-- the move brings a second conversion from its date; for one who moved in
-- תשס"ח, also one completed from 1.1.08 to 31.8.08.
@ref akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_4 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_5 akn:art_44__para_b__subpara_6
GIVEN w IS A `when the entitlement was completed`
GIVETH A `how a new degree or training allowance counts`
DECIDE `how the new entitlement counts` w IS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `by March of the year before the move` THEN `in X from the start`
    WHEN `between March and 1 September of the year of the move` THEN `in X from the start`
    WHEN `between 1 September and 31 December of the year of the move` THEN `in X by a second conversion, from the date of the entitlement`
    WHEN `between 1.1.08 and 31.8.08, the teacher having moved in 5768` THEN `in X by a second conversion, from the date of the entitlement`
    WHEN `later` THEN `not in X`

GIVEN `amount of each component` IS A FUNCTION FROM `pay component` TO NUMBER, components IS A LIST OF `pay component`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `X, the salary to convert` `amount of each component` components IS
    sum (map `amount of each component` (filter `in the salary to convert` components))

§§ `44(ג) Y, the conversion coefficient`

DECLARE `status` IS ONE OF
    `a regular teacher`
    `a mother teacher`
    `a homeroom teacher`
    `a homeroom teacher and mother`

DECLARE `position base` IS ONE OF
    `the primary base of 30 weekly hours`
    `the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours`

-- (ג) ¶1–¶21: the addition, in percent, for one on a single position base,
-- by status and the school he will work in. ¶22: in a special-education
-- school of several stages, the base is the one he was on, on the eve of
-- the move; ¶23: for the teachers of §10(א)–(ב), the status is §10(ג)'s.
-- Both are what the inputs `s` and `b` are taken from.
@ref akn:art_44__para_c akn:art_44__para_c/p2 akn:art_44__para_c/p3 akn:art_44__para_c/p4 akn:art_44__para_c/p5 akn:art_44__para_c/p6 akn:art_44__para_c/p7 akn:art_44__para_c/p8 akn:art_44__para_c/p9 akn:art_44__para_c/p10 akn:art_44__para_c/p11 akn:art_44__para_c/p12 akn:art_44__para_c/p13 akn:art_44__para_c/p14 akn:art_44__para_c/p15 akn:art_44__para_c/p16 akn:art_44__para_c/p17 akn:art_44__para_c/p18 akn:art_44__para_c/p19 akn:art_44__para_c/p20 akn:art_44__para_c/p21 akn:art_44__para_c/p22 akn:art_44__para_c/p23
GIVEN s IS A `status`, b IS A `position base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y on a single base` s b IS
    (CONSIDER s
     WHEN `a regular teacher`             THEN 17
     WHEN `a mother teacher`              THEN 24
     WHEN `a homeroom teacher`            THEN 20
     WHEN `a homeroom teacher and mother` THEN 27)
    PLUS (IF b EQUALS `the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours` THEN 10 ELSE 0)

-- ¶24–¶29: on two bases, Y = H × (the junior-high addition) + S × (the
-- primary addition), H and S the shares of the whole position on each,
-- even above 100%.
@ref akn:art_44__para_c/p24 akn:art_44__para_c/p25 akn:art_44__para_c/p26 akn:art_44__para_c/p27 akn:art_44__para_c/p28 akn:art_44__para_c/p29
GIVEN s IS A `status`, `position on the 24-hour base` IS A NUMBER, `position on the 30-hour base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y on two bases` s `position on the 24-hour base` `position on the 30-hour base` IS
    (    `position on the 24-hour base` TIMES `Y on a single base` s `the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours`
     PLUS `position on the 30-hour base` TIMES `Y on a single base` s `the primary base of 30 weekly hours`)
    DIVIDED BY (`position on the 24-hour base` PLUS `position on the 30-hour base`)

-- The example (¶30–¶35): a regular teacher of 110%, 70% on the 30-hour
-- base and 40% on the 24-hour one: (40/110 × 27) + (70/110 × 17) = 20.64.
@ref akn:art_44__para_c/p30 akn:art_44__para_c/p31 akn:art_44__para_c/p32 akn:art_44__para_c/p33 akn:art_44__para_c/p34 akn:art_44__para_c/p35
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`Y on two bases` `a regular teacher` 0.4 0.7) EQUALS 20.64

§§ `44(ד) A`

-- (ד): A = X × (100 + Y)%. No rounding is stated (convention
-- rounding.default).
@ref akn:art_44__para_d akn:art_44__para_d/p2
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `A, the converted pay` x y IS
    x TIMES (100 PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- The table's columns: the junior-high addition is the primary one plus 10.
#ASSERT `Y on a single base` `a homeroom teacher and mother` `the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours` EQUALS 37
#ASSERT `Y on a single base` `a mother teacher` `the primary base of 30 weekly hours` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `A, the converted pay` 7000 17 EQUALS 8190
#ASSERT `in the salary to convert` `a trailing management or counselling allowance`
#ASSERT NOT `in the salary to convert` `a role allowance §39 keeps`
-- One base alone gives that base's Y.
#ASSERT `Y on two bases` `a homeroom teacher` 0 1 EQUALS 20
